WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.130
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.400 --> 01:34.950
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.200 --> 01:37.780
[Episode 50]

4
01:39.310 --> 01:42.000
On November 2, 1935,

5
01:42.210 --> 01:44.720
the CPC Central Committee, leading the Shaanxi-Gansu Detachment,

6
01:44.720 --> 01:46.160
arrived in Xiasiwan

7
01:46.700 --> 01:49.759
and held a Politburo meeting the following day.

8
01:50.450 --> 01:51.780
The meeting decided

9
01:51.990 --> 01:53.820
to establish the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission

10
01:53.820 --> 01:56.479
of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army,

11
01:56.500 --> 01:58.370
with Mao Zedong as Chairman

12
01:58.390 --> 02:01.110
and Zhou Enlai and Peng Dehuai as Vice Chairmen.

13
02:01.580 --> 02:04.010
The designation of the 1st Front Red Army was restored,

14
02:04.010 --> 02:05.700
with Peng Dehuai as Commander

15
02:06.060 --> 02:08.259
and Mao Zedong as Political Commissar.

16
02:08.530 --> 02:11.990
It comprised the 1st Red Army Corps and the 15th Red Army Corps.

17
02:12.370 --> 02:13.460
Following the reorganization,

18
02:13.460 --> 02:15.320
the 1st Front Red Army had a total strength

19
02:15.320 --> 02:16.579
of over 10,000 troops.

20
02:17.530 --> 02:18.970
While in Xiasiwan,

21
02:19.530 --> 02:21.500
Mao Zedong and other Central Committee leaders

22
02:21.500 --> 02:22.640
made detailed inquiries into

23
02:22.640 --> 02:25.500
the anti-counterrevolutionary campaign in the Shaanxi-Gansu Soviet Area.

24
02:25.500 --> 02:27.690
They immediately dispatched Wang Shoudao, Jia Tuofu,

25
02:27.690 --> 02:29.090
Liu Xiangsan, and others

26
02:29.340 --> 02:32.500
to the Shaanxi-Gansu-Shanxi Provincial Committee headquarters

27
02:32.500 --> 02:33.570
in Wayaobu

28
02:33.850 --> 02:36.310
to take over the Northwest Security Bureau.

29
02:36.970 --> 02:38.370
On November 10,

30
02:38.570 --> 02:41.230
the Party's Central organs arrived in Wayaobu.

31
02:41.300 --> 02:44.220
A 5-member Party Affairs Committee was immediately formed,

32
02:44.220 --> 02:46.510
including Dong Biwu and Wang Shoudao.

33
02:47.220 --> 02:48.680
Under Bo Gu's guidance,

34
02:48.850 --> 02:51.370
it reviewed the wrongful anti-counterrevolutionary cases.

35
02:51.370 --> 02:53.900
Zhang Wentian, as the Central Committee's top official,

36
02:53.900 --> 02:55.700
personally oversaw the review.

37
02:56.460 --> 02:58.320
After a thorough investigation,

38
02:58.530 --> 02:59.970
the Central Committee concluded

39
02:59.970 --> 03:02.410
that the arrests of Comrades Liu Zhidan, Xi Zhongxun, and others

40
03:02.410 --> 03:04.210
had been entirely unjustified.

41
03:04.410 --> 03:05.940
It ordered the release of those

42
03:05.940 --> 03:07.870
who had been wrongfully detained.

43
03:08.220 --> 03:10.460
On November 26, it issued

44
03:10.500 --> 03:13.810
the Decision of the Northwest Central Bureau on Reviewing the Anti-counterrevolutionary Campaign,

45
03:13.810 --> 03:17.530
officially rehabilitating Liu Zhidan, Xi Zhongxun, and others.

46
03:20.400 --> 03:22.040
I've told you so many times.

47
03:20.470 --> 03:26.700
[Xiasiwan, Ganquan County, Shaanxi]

48
03:22.340 --> 03:24.460
Don't stay up so late at night.

49
03:24.640 --> 03:26.329
You already have trouble sleeping.

50
03:26.329 --> 03:28.400
Look how thick your glasses are.

51
03:28.570 --> 03:30.250
How much thicker do you want them to get?

52
03:30.250 --> 03:32.980
I've told you so many times, but you never listen.

53
03:34.370 --> 03:36.620
I wish I could go to bed earlier, too.

54
03:37.410 --> 03:38.340
But tell me,

55
03:38.530 --> 03:41.460
when the documents come in, how can I not review them?

56
03:41.740 --> 03:43.180
I know the lighting is poor, too.

57
03:43.180 --> 03:44.650
My prescription is already strong enough.

58
03:43.230 --> 03:46.140
[Liu Ying, Head of the Publicity Department of the Central Committee of the Communist Youth League]

59
03:45.370 --> 03:47.300
But there's so much work to deal with.

60
03:47.300 --> 03:48.340
I need to get everything in order.

61
03:48.340 --> 03:50.190
I have to do my duty.

62
03:52.470 --> 03:53.880
Still, Comrade Liu Ying,

63
03:54.340 --> 03:56.270
I'll take your criticism to heart.

64
03:56.420 --> 03:59.280
From now on, you're in charge of keeping an eye on me.

65
03:59.370 --> 04:00.570
You just give the orders.

66
04:00.570 --> 04:02.300
I'll follow them to the letter.

67
04:02.630 --> 04:04.160
What are you talking about?

68
04:07.070 --> 04:07.960
Have a date.

69
04:08.240 --> 04:09.570
That'll keep you quiet.

70
04:09.570 --> 04:10.570
Honestly!

71
04:38.670 --> 04:39.730
What are you doing?

72
04:47.370 --> 04:48.330
The Chairman.

73
04:49.240 --> 04:49.890
Did they see that?

74
04:49.890 --> 04:50.960
How would I know if they saw that or not?

75
04:50.960 --> 04:51.890
So, did they see that or not?

76
04:51.890 --> 04:53.390
I don't know. Why were you copying me?

77
04:53.390 --> 04:54.420
Well, I just saw how happy you were,

78
04:54.420 --> 04:54.890
so I...

79
04:55.420 --> 04:56.330
Chairman!

80
04:57.980 --> 04:58.600
Luofu.

81
04:59.180 --> 05:00.060
Comrade Luofu.

82
05:00.130 --> 05:01.330
Greetings, leaders!

83
05:02.180 --> 05:03.870
Comrade Liu Ying, you're here, too.

84
05:03.870 --> 05:05.590
Comrade Liu Ying, you're here, too.

85
05:05.590 --> 05:07.790
Oh, Comrade Liu Ying, you're here, too.

86
05:09.060 --> 05:09.420
It's all right.

87
05:09.420 --> 05:10.250
It's almost time for the meeting anyway.

88
05:10.250 --> 05:11.010
Let's get started.

89
05:11.010 --> 05:12.740
I'll, I'll pour you some water.

90
05:18.940 --> 05:21.690
It's not really a formal meeting.

91
05:21.890 --> 05:25.570
We're just gathering to say goodbye.

92
05:26.130 --> 05:28.100
It's a farewell, but also a celebration.

93
05:28.100 --> 05:30.560
A celebration of the successful conclusion

94
05:30.740 --> 05:31.810
of our Politburo meeting.

95
05:31.810 --> 05:33.010
A celebration of the establishment of the Northwest Central Bureau

96
05:33.010 --> 05:35.890
and the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission.

97
05:35.890 --> 05:38.690
And of the restoration of the 1st Front Red Army's designation.

98
05:38.690 --> 05:39.620
Speaking of farewells...

99
05:39.620 --> 05:40.130
Careful, it's hot.

100
05:40.130 --> 05:41.810
Tomorrow, Comrades Zedong,

101
05:41.940 --> 05:43.740
Enlai, and Peng Dehuai

102
05:43.980 --> 05:46.420
will lead the 1st Army Corps south

103
05:46.500 --> 05:48.659
to join forces with the 15th Army Corps.

104
05:48.659 --> 05:51.210
The three of us also need to return to Wayaobu

105
05:51.370 --> 05:53.950
to oversee rear-area affairs in the Soviet region.

106
05:53.950 --> 05:54.750
That's right.

107
05:55.260 --> 05:57.460
It's both a farewell and a celebration.

108
05:58.450 --> 06:00.510
Too bad we don't have any food or wine.

109
06:01.990 --> 06:03.450
Let's drink to each other with water instead.

110
06:03.450 --> 06:04.540
A toast with water. Come on.

111
06:04.540 --> 06:05.210
Come on.

112
06:05.450 --> 06:06.290
Come on.

113
06:15.510 --> 06:16.220
Luofu.

114
06:17.740 --> 06:18.780
No food or wine,

115
06:19.060 --> 06:20.520
but you've got dates here?

116
06:20.700 --> 06:22.140
Is this your date pit?

117
06:22.250 --> 06:24.980
Yes. It's a dog-head date from Northern Shaanxi.

118
06:25.180 --> 06:26.130
Where did you get it?

119
06:26.130 --> 06:28.100
Who gave it to you? Is it good?

120
06:28.210 --> 06:29.090
It's delicious.

121
06:29.090 --> 06:31.450
No, you still haven't told us where it came from.

122
06:31.450 --> 06:32.250
That's right.

123
06:33.860 --> 06:34.770
I gave it to him.

124
06:36.570 --> 06:37.540
-You gave it to him? -You gave it to him?

125
06:37.540 --> 06:38.980
I've been having trouble sleeping.

126
06:38.980 --> 06:41.210
So Comrade Liu Ying gave me a date.

127
06:42.620 --> 06:44.890
Comrade Enlai has trouble sleeping, too.

128
06:44.890 --> 06:45.770
Are there any more?

129
06:45.770 --> 06:46.500
Any more?

130
06:46.659 --> 06:47.500
Got any left?

131
06:50.940 --> 06:51.690
Any at all?

132
06:52.070 --> 06:52.950
Only two.

133
06:53.940 --> 06:54.860
Only two?

134
06:54.990 --> 06:57.650
Two? Then one for each of you?

135
06:58.770 --> 07:00.030
Oh, one for each of you?

136
07:01.250 --> 07:02.000
One each?

137
07:07.060 --> 07:08.210
All right, all right.

138
07:08.210 --> 07:09.470
I'll stop teasing you.

139
07:09.860 --> 07:11.100
But Luofu.

140
07:11.860 --> 07:12.860
Comrade Liu Ying.

141
07:13.420 --> 07:15.950
I've played matchmaker for you two all the way

142
07:16.170 --> 07:17.620
from Jiangxi to northern Shaanxi.

143
07:17.620 --> 07:21.150
I've been keeping this match alive for over 10,000 kilometers!

144
07:21.420 --> 07:23.900
So today, I want to ask you both outright.

145
07:24.860 --> 07:27.020
When are you going to

146
07:27.450 --> 07:30.370
treat us all to a wedding feast?

147
07:31.060 --> 07:32.330
Give us a straight answer.

148
07:32.330 --> 07:33.730
No dodging the question.

149
07:34.940 --> 07:35.860
I... Well, I...

150
07:36.100 --> 07:38.230
Comrade Liu Ying, where are you going?

151
07:39.090 --> 07:39.680
I...

152
07:43.740 --> 07:46.130
I think everyone already knows how I feel...

153
07:46.130 --> 07:46.740
Your feelings...

154
07:46.740 --> 07:48.180
We all know how you feel.

155
07:48.200 --> 07:50.460
I want to hear Comrade Liu Ying's answer.

156
07:50.909 --> 07:51.909
Comrade Liu Ying?

157
07:56.810 --> 07:57.860
I think...

158
07:58.420 --> 08:01.550
We should probably wait until we've settled down first.

159
08:04.010 --> 08:06.010
That's a very remarkable answer.

160
08:06.740 --> 08:07.570
That's right.

161
08:08.540 --> 08:10.130
Now that we've reached northern Shaanxi,

162
08:10.130 --> 08:12.500
both for the sake of our work and our personal lives,

163
08:12.500 --> 08:14.540
we need to get settled first.

164
08:17.060 --> 08:18.390
But don't wait too long!

165
08:18.540 --> 08:19.470
Soon, all right?

166
08:19.540 --> 08:20.420
Soon!

167
08:20.560 --> 08:21.330
As soon as possible.

168
08:21.330 --> 08:22.460
As soon as possible.

169
08:24.180 --> 08:25.180
All right, all right.

170
08:25.180 --> 08:26.540
Well, we'd better get going.

171
08:26.540 --> 08:27.680
All right. I'll see you out.

172
08:27.680 --> 08:28.240
Sure.

173
08:33.260 --> 08:33.809
Come on.

174
08:38.020 --> 08:38.950
Comrade Zedong.

175
08:39.330 --> 08:41.020
I wish you all the best.

176
08:41.179 --> 08:41.780
Thank you.

177
08:42.539 --> 08:44.059
Everything will be fine.

178
08:44.210 --> 08:44.810
All right.

179
08:44.810 --> 08:45.410
We're off.

180
08:45.810 --> 08:46.410
Take care.

181
08:50.180 --> 08:52.710
We'll be waiting for your triumphant return.

182
08:53.810 --> 08:54.540
Look!

183
08:54.610 --> 08:56.440
This is all your fault! All your fault!

184
08:56.440 --> 08:58.570
The Chairman and the others all saw it!

185
09:15.330 --> 09:17.730
On November 5, 1935.

186
09:18.020 --> 09:20.260
Mao Zedong, Zhou Enlai, and Peng Dehuai

187
09:20.260 --> 09:21.730
led the 1st Red Army Corps

188
09:21.780 --> 09:24.210
to Xiangbizaiwan, Ganquan County.

189
09:23.080 --> 09:28.350
[Xiangbizaiwan, Ganquan County, Shaanxi]

190
09:24.730 --> 09:25.970
They rested there

191
09:25.990 --> 09:29.450
while awaiting their rendezvous with the 15th Red Army Corps.

192
09:33.490 --> 09:34.300
Mao,

193
09:34.770 --> 09:35.850
have you finished preparing the speech

194
09:35.850 --> 09:37.110
for the 1st Army Corps?

195
09:39.670 --> 09:41.730
You haven't even started writing it?

196
09:49.090 --> 09:51.330
I don't know where to begin.

197
09:54.270 --> 09:56.070
Have a seat. Everyone, sit down.

198
10:00.710 --> 10:02.970
I've been doing some figuring in my head.

199
10:03.690 --> 10:04.540
Figuring?

200
10:06.660 --> 10:09.840
Counting from the day the Central Red Army set out

201
10:10.450 --> 10:12.110
until our victorious arrival

202
10:12.970 --> 10:14.570
in northern Shaanxi,

203
10:16.570 --> 10:18.230
we were on the march for a total

204
10:18.810 --> 10:20.260
of 367 days.

205
10:20.900 --> 10:21.930
We spent

206
10:22.730 --> 10:24.540
approximately 35 days in combat.

207
10:24.540 --> 10:26.340
The number of days spent resting

208
10:26.690 --> 10:27.950
was no more than 65.

209
10:28.810 --> 10:30.210
We spent

210
10:30.570 --> 10:32.100
about 267 days on the march.

211
10:32.370 --> 10:34.230
And if we count the night marches,

212
10:34.510 --> 10:36.510
the number was even higher than 267.

213
10:37.730 --> 10:39.330
We covered all that distance

214
10:39.810 --> 10:41.850
with our own two feet,

215
10:42.020 --> 10:44.380
wearing nothing but straw sandals.

216
10:46.260 --> 10:47.140
That's right.

217
10:47.610 --> 10:49.140
Wearing straw sandals,

218
10:49.780 --> 10:51.310
we crossed the Five Ridges,

219
10:51.660 --> 10:52.610
Loushanguan,

220
10:53.490 --> 10:54.820
the Daliang Mountains,

221
10:55.180 --> 10:56.380
and Liupan Mountain.

222
10:56.850 --> 10:59.180
We crossed the Xiang River, the Wujiang River,

223
10:59.180 --> 11:01.610
the Jinsha River and the Dadu River.

224
11:02.060 --> 11:04.260
We climbed over snow-capped mountains

225
11:04.380 --> 11:06.380
and trekked across the grasslands.

226
11:06.380 --> 11:09.810
We traveled through Jiangxi, Fujian,

227
11:10.730 --> 11:13.520
Guangdong, Hunan, Guangxi,

228
11:14.450 --> 11:16.490
Guizhou, Yunnan, Sichuan,

229
11:16.810 --> 11:19.450
Xikang, Gansu, and Shaanxi,

230
11:19.540 --> 11:20.780
11 provinces in all.

231
11:21.420 --> 11:23.480
The troops that marched the farthest

232
11:24.660 --> 11:26.980
covered 12,500 kilometers.

233
11:41.850 --> 11:45.170
This was truly a Long March!

234
11:46.690 --> 11:48.270
From the dawn of creation,

235
11:49.880 --> 11:51.940
from the Three Sovereigns and Five Emperors to this day,

236
11:51.940 --> 11:52.730
tell me,

237
11:54.020 --> 11:56.350
has there ever been a Long March like this?

238
11:56.420 --> 11:57.060
No!

239
11:58.490 --> 11:59.690
Never!

240
12:00.690 --> 12:02.610
In all of human history,

241
12:02.780 --> 12:06.030
there has never been such a feat!

242
12:07.300 --> 12:08.570
Along the way,

243
12:09.390 --> 12:11.060
we forged an ironclad army.

244
12:11.810 --> 12:12.780
This army

245
12:13.420 --> 12:14.610
is invincible.

246
12:14.850 --> 12:16.420
Just like in that poem you wrote

247
12:16.420 --> 12:17.730
on Liupan Mountain:

248
12:17.930 --> 12:20.060
"With the long rope in our hands today,

249
12:20.150 --> 12:22.500
when shall we bind the Azure Dragon?"

250
12:22.780 --> 12:23.540
Excellent!

251
12:24.090 --> 12:24.730
Mao,

252
12:25.490 --> 12:26.730
you should tell them all about it.

253
12:26.730 --> 12:27.970
Tell everyone

254
12:28.380 --> 12:29.570
about this miracle!

255
12:29.690 --> 12:30.490
That's right.

256
12:30.710 --> 12:32.570
The comrades have all assembled.

257
12:33.950 --> 12:34.500
Okay.

258
12:36.870 --> 12:39.530
This miracle wasn't achieved through my words.

259
12:39.610 --> 12:42.260
It was created by all of us together.

260
12:42.540 --> 12:43.200
Let's go.

261
12:46.060 --> 12:48.450
On November 5, 1935,

262
12:48.860 --> 12:50.700
at Xiangbizaiwan,

263
12:50.720 --> 12:53.490
Mao Zedong delivered his famous "Snowfield Speech"

264
12:53.490 --> 12:56.610
to more than 300 officers and soldiers of the troops accompanying him.

265
12:56.610 --> 12:58.380
In his speech, he said,

266
12:58.730 --> 13:00.610
"The Long March is a manifesto.

267
13:01.090 --> 13:02.850
It proclaims to the whole world

268
13:02.970 --> 13:05.030
that the Red Army is a force of heroes.

269
13:05.260 --> 13:06.730
It declares that Chiang Kai-shek's attempts

270
13:06.730 --> 13:09.390
to encircle and pursue us have ended in failure.

271
13:09.690 --> 13:12.140
The Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army has triumphed!

272
13:12.140 --> 13:14.000
The Chinese Revolution has hope!

273
13:14.540 --> 13:16.610
The Long March is a publicity campaign.

274
13:16.610 --> 13:18.890
We spread the word as we marched,

275
13:19.140 --> 13:21.490
taking our message wherever we went.

276
13:22.060 --> 13:24.420
We mobilized and organized the people,

277
13:24.570 --> 13:26.610
confiscated the landlords' wealth and redistributed their land.

278
13:26.610 --> 13:27.900
We proclaimed to the 200 million people

279
13:27.900 --> 13:29.730
across 11 provinces

280
13:30.090 --> 13:31.610
that only the Red Army's path

281
13:31.610 --> 13:33.470
could liberate the poor.

282
13:33.990 --> 13:36.250
The Long March is a seed-sowing machine.

283
13:36.590 --> 13:38.420
The seeds of revolution it scattered

284
13:38.420 --> 13:40.420
would take root along the Red Army's

285
13:40.430 --> 13:41.980
route, sprout,

286
13:42.010 --> 13:43.410
blossom, and bear fruit.

287
13:43.970 --> 13:44.830
Wherever we go,

288
13:44.930 --> 13:47.420
we will sow the seeds of revolution.

289
13:47.900 --> 13:50.360
And they will surely yield a great harvest."

290
13:51.420 --> 13:52.780
Meanwhile, far away,

291
13:53.150 --> 13:54.140
at the very same time Mao Zedong

292
13:54.140 --> 13:56.260
was delivering his "Snowfield Speech,"

293
13:55.360 --> 14:03.260
[Shanghai; Soviet Consulate General in Shanghai]

294
13:56.540 --> 13:58.810
more than 1,000 kilometers away, in Shanghai,

295
13:58.810 --> 14:01.160
several prominent figures, filled with patriotic fervor,

296
14:01.160 --> 14:02.330
who sympathized with and supported

297
14:02.330 --> 14:04.540
the Communist Party of China,

298
14:04.940 --> 14:08.180
were following the Red Army's great achievement.

299
14:22.670 --> 14:25.800
[Bogomolov, Soviet Ambassador to China]

300
14:25.840 --> 14:29.340
[Soong Ching-ling]

301
15:36.730 --> 15:37.660
Mr. Lu Xun,

302
15:37.850 --> 15:40.940
what do you think of this film?

303
15:42.570 --> 15:43.900
It's an excellent film.

304
15:44.570 --> 15:47.130
The Soviet Union has people like Chapaev.

305
15:47.660 --> 15:50.570
That gives the country hope.

306
15:50.100 --> 15:53.870
[Lu Xun]

307
15:51.020 --> 15:52.090
Mr. Ambassador,

308
15:53.490 --> 15:55.270
China today

309
15:55.130 --> 15:57.200
[Agnes Smedley, American Progressive Journalist]

310
15:55.480 --> 15:58.630
also has thousands of men like Chapaev

311
15:58.690 --> 15:59.970
fighting for their country.

312
15:59.970 --> 16:01.850
I've had the good fortune to meet some of them.

313
16:01.770 --> 16:05.740
[Mao Dun]

314
16:02.080 --> 16:05.720
They are now marching westward.

315
16:06.330 --> 16:07.260
Mr. Ambassador,

316
16:07.540 --> 16:09.020
among those marching west

317
16:09.140 --> 16:11.570
are several fighters from the cultural world:

318
16:11.570 --> 16:12.370
Feng Xuefeng,

319
16:12.380 --> 16:13.180
Cheng Fangwu,

320
16:13.450 --> 16:15.450
and my former superior, Mao Zedong.

321
16:15.680 --> 16:16.390
Indeed.

322
16:16.820 --> 16:20.300
And there's also Liao Chengzhi, son of Madam He Xiangning.

323
16:20.390 --> 16:22.420
[He Xiangning, Wife of Liao Zhongkai]

324
16:20.810 --> 16:22.780
I also think of Deng Yingchao.

325
16:22.970 --> 16:24.490
During the Great Revolution,

326
16:24.490 --> 16:26.020
she and Mr. Zhou Enlai

327
16:26.300 --> 16:28.160
were frequent guests at our home.

328
16:28.380 --> 16:29.610
You may not know this,

329
16:29.810 --> 16:31.540
but Deng Yingchao and Mengxing

330
16:31.610 --> 16:34.060
were born on the very same day.

331
16:34.300 --> 16:35.940
She even calls me "Mother."

332
16:37.060 --> 16:38.380
Mengxing and Chengzhi

333
16:38.570 --> 16:41.810
have always called Zhou Enlai "Brother."

334
16:41.850 --> 16:44.710
I wonder where they are now.

335
16:46.810 --> 16:48.760
Mr. Lu Xun once said,

336
16:50.090 --> 16:52.140
"The world had no roads to begin with.

337
16:52.140 --> 16:54.850
When enough people walk it, a road appears."

338
16:55.490 --> 16:56.490
No matter what,

339
16:56.780 --> 16:59.450
as long as there's a road, there's a future.

340
17:00.060 --> 17:00.810
And besides,

341
17:01.060 --> 17:02.660
among those blazing the trail

342
17:02.660 --> 17:04.730
are men like Mao Zedong,

343
17:04.730 --> 17:06.619
a Chapaev who can write poetry.

344
17:06.770 --> 17:09.260
With them clearing the way,

345
17:09.280 --> 17:12.560
they will surely forge a path to victory.

346
17:17.420 --> 17:19.690
You've all seen the August 1 Declaration issued

347
17:19.690 --> 17:21.490
by the Communist Party of China.

348
17:24.940 --> 17:26.940
All the Chapaevs of China

349
17:27.140 --> 17:28.339
will unite with the entire Chinese people

350
17:28.339 --> 17:31.000
to lead the fight against Japanese aggression.

351
17:35.290 --> 17:36.290
Mr. Lu Xun,

352
17:37.050 --> 17:40.100
your health seems to be getting worse.

353
17:40.250 --> 17:41.530
I'm very worried.

354
17:42.620 --> 17:46.420
The struggle is far from over.

355
17:46.770 --> 17:48.380
A true fighter

356
17:48.580 --> 17:50.580
keeps moving forward,

357
17:50.770 --> 17:52.100
even covered in wounds.

358
17:52.490 --> 17:54.820
Among these Chapaevs,

359
17:55.100 --> 17:58.100
a Red Army division commander named Chen Geng told me

360
17:58.290 --> 18:00.380
that on the battlefield, they live by one rule:

361
18:00.380 --> 18:02.380
"Minor wounds are no reason to leave the front."

362
18:02.380 --> 18:04.820
I, too, must keep fighting.

363
18:18.940 --> 18:20.410
Corps Commander, you're back.

364
18:20.410 --> 18:21.100
Has Chairman Mao arrived?

365
18:21.100 --> 18:21.860
Yes, he's inside.

366
18:21.860 --> 18:22.990
All right, go ahead.

367
18:28.760 --> 18:30.200
No, no. Just listen.

368
18:29.010 --> 18:31.980
[Xu Haidong, Commander of the 15th Red Army Corps]

369
18:31.290 --> 18:32.730
Reporting to you, Chairman!

370
18:32.730 --> 18:34.420
I'm Xu Haidong of the 15th Red Army Corps!

371
18:34.420 --> 18:35.150
How was that?

372
18:37.100 --> 18:37.770
Not bad?

373
18:38.530 --> 18:39.210
Go on.

374
18:39.660 --> 18:40.420
Wait, wait!

375
18:40.770 --> 18:41.770
One more version.

376
18:42.450 --> 18:42.970
Reporting to you, Chairman!

377
18:42.970 --> 18:46.100
Xu Haidong of the 15th Red Army Corps reporting for duty!

378
18:46.140 --> 18:46.860
Well?

379
18:47.940 --> 18:48.770
Which one was better?

380
18:48.770 --> 18:49.630
The second one.

381
18:49.820 --> 18:50.680
The second one.

382
18:51.010 --> 18:51.620
The second one?

383
18:51.620 --> 18:52.450
The second one!

384
18:52.450 --> 18:52.980
Go ahead.

385
19:11.100 --> 19:12.230
Comrade Xu Haidong,

386
19:13.860 --> 19:14.770
I'm Mao Zedong.

387
19:23.100 --> 19:24.100
Comrade Haidong,

388
19:24.770 --> 19:26.230
you've been through a lot.

389
19:33.310 --> 19:34.430
[Cheng Zihua, Political Commissar of the 15th Red Army Corps]

390
19:34.140 --> 19:35.140
Comrade Haidong,

391
19:35.210 --> 19:37.730
haven't you been looking forward to meeting Chairman Mao every day?

392
19:37.730 --> 19:38.490
Now that he's right here,

393
19:38.490 --> 19:40.290
why aren't you saying anything?

394
19:41.050 --> 19:43.010
Well, it's just that I'm so happy.

395
19:43.300 --> 19:44.040
Greetings, Chairman Mao!

396
19:44.040 --> 19:45.360
Good, good!

397
19:46.820 --> 19:47.770
I never imagined

398
19:47.790 --> 19:49.730
that Xu Haidong, who strikes fear into the enemy,

399
19:49.730 --> 19:51.290
and whom Generalissimo Chiang himself called

400
19:51.290 --> 19:53.730
"one of the greatest scourges of civilization,"

401
19:53.730 --> 19:54.860
the fearsome "Tiger Xu,"

402
19:54.860 --> 19:57.390
would turn out to be such a simple, honest man.

403
19:58.660 --> 19:59.580
Reporting to you, Chairman.

404
19:59.580 --> 20:01.910
I was directing the battle at Zhangcunyi.

405
20:02.180 --> 20:04.050
The political commissar sent someone with a message.

406
20:04.050 --> 20:06.310
There were 3 matches taped to the letter.

407
20:06.580 --> 20:07.250
I thought

408
20:07.560 --> 20:08.900
there must be some urgent military situation.

409
20:08.900 --> 20:10.030
But when I opened it,

410
20:10.350 --> 20:11.440
I saw it was news that you were coming.

411
20:11.440 --> 20:12.950
So I rushed over here right away.

412
20:12.950 --> 20:14.510
I had 5 matches taped to it,

413
20:14.690 --> 20:15.770
but I was afraid you'd get too anxious,

414
20:15.770 --> 20:16.820
so I took 2 off.

415
20:18.380 --> 20:20.040
Come on. Let me introduce you.

416
20:20.100 --> 20:21.700
This is Comrade Peng Dehuai.

417
20:22.100 --> 20:23.960
Good to meet you, Commander Peng!

418
20:24.130 --> 20:25.890
Comrade Haidong, do you know?

419
20:26.010 --> 20:27.600
Chiang Kai-shek has put a price of 100,000 silver dollars

420
20:27.600 --> 20:28.470
on your head.

421
20:28.530 --> 20:30.450
The same price as my head.

422
20:32.740 --> 20:34.660
Chairman, please sit down and have some water.

423
20:34.660 --> 20:36.100
Yes, yes. Come, sit down.

424
20:36.100 --> 20:36.860
-Come on. -All right.

425
20:36.860 --> 20:37.490
Please, have a seat.

426
20:37.490 --> 20:37.820
Come on.

427
20:37.820 --> 20:38.650
Come, sit down.

428
20:38.650 --> 20:39.900
Let me pour you some water.

429
20:39.900 --> 20:40.900
You've been riding for so long.

430
20:40.900 --> 20:41.860
We can pour it ourselves.

431
20:41.860 --> 20:43.960
You're our leader. How can I let you do it?

432
20:43.960 --> 20:45.050
I'll do it. Let me.

433
20:45.090 --> 20:46.120
No need to be so formal.

434
20:46.120 --> 20:47.850
After all, we're all comrades.

435
20:47.900 --> 20:48.820
We're one family.

436
20:48.820 --> 20:51.010
It doesn't matter who pours. I'll do it.

437
20:51.010 --> 20:53.340
No, no, no. Especially not you, Chairman.

438
20:53.490 --> 20:54.860
Please, sit down. Sit down.

439
20:54.860 --> 20:55.620
I'll do it. Thank you.

440
20:55.620 --> 20:58.010
Chairman, what you just said is absolutely right.

441
20:58.010 --> 20:59.100
We are one family.

442
20:59.410 --> 21:01.210
But it's been so hard

443
21:02.530 --> 21:04.390
for this family to come together.

444
21:05.250 --> 21:06.400
It's been over 3 years

445
21:06.400 --> 21:09.470
since the 4th Front Red Army

446
21:09.970 --> 21:11.690
left the Hubei-Henan-Anhui Base.

447
21:11.690 --> 21:13.010
Over those 3 years,

448
21:13.870 --> 21:14.980
our 25th Red Army

449
21:15.010 --> 21:18.410
went through several reorganizations and restructurings.

450
21:18.420 --> 21:19.290
After arriving in northern Shaanxi,

451
21:19.290 --> 21:22.100
we formed the 15th Red Army Corps.

452
21:22.210 --> 21:23.470
Throughout that time,

453
21:24.290 --> 21:26.820
we've had to fight almost entirely on our own.

454
21:28.010 --> 21:29.530
But things are different now.

455
21:29.530 --> 21:30.530
You've come.

456
21:31.010 --> 21:33.250
Now we have the Central Committee leading us.

457
21:33.250 --> 21:35.650
Comrade Haidong, I admire your frankness.

458
21:36.140 --> 21:37.540
Your words truly move us.

459
21:37.940 --> 21:40.400
We brought the 1st Army Corps south this time

460
21:40.530 --> 21:41.860
to join forces with you.

461
21:42.010 --> 21:45.010
We want our 2 corps to fight side by side,

462
21:45.140 --> 21:47.180
break the enemy's encirclement campaigns,

463
21:47.180 --> 21:48.900
link our base areas together,

464
21:49.450 --> 21:50.860
and consolidate them.

465
21:50.900 --> 21:53.420
That will give us a base from which to resist Japanese aggression.

466
21:53.420 --> 21:54.480
That's wonderful!

467
21:54.530 --> 21:55.660
Comrade Haidong,

468
21:55.820 --> 21:57.660
we've brought you a radio transmitter this time

469
21:57.660 --> 21:59.390
so you can stay in touch with us.

470
21:59.940 --> 22:00.870
Commander Peng,

471
22:00.970 --> 22:01.900
well, we...

472
22:01.900 --> 22:02.420
Please, sit down. Sit.

473
22:02.420 --> 22:03.100
Let's talk sitting down.

474
22:03.100 --> 22:04.300
All right, all right.

475
22:04.820 --> 22:07.100
We've indeed been without a radio all this time,

476
22:07.100 --> 22:08.690
because none of us knows how to operate one.

477
22:08.690 --> 22:10.340
We've had to rely on cavalry to deliver messages.

478
22:10.340 --> 22:11.470
That's far too slow.

479
22:12.010 --> 22:13.820
Our base area is still relatively small.

480
22:13.820 --> 22:15.580
But once it expands,

481
22:15.820 --> 22:17.380
your couriers won't be able to keep up

482
22:17.380 --> 22:19.370
delivering messages on horseback.

483
22:19.370 --> 22:20.100
Don't worry.

484
22:20.140 --> 22:22.490
This time, we've brought you not only a radio,

485
22:22.490 --> 22:24.180
but also a radio operator.

486
22:25.580 --> 22:27.380
Whenever you need to contact us,

487
22:27.460 --> 22:28.250
just tell him.

488
22:28.250 --> 22:28.940
Good.

489
22:29.940 --> 22:30.580
Then...

490
22:31.140 --> 22:32.290
I'll take it back with me.

491
22:32.290 --> 22:33.860
Once we've taken Zhangcunyi,

492
22:33.860 --> 22:35.250
the first telegram I'll send

493
22:35.250 --> 22:36.450
will be to share the good news with you.

494
22:36.450 --> 22:37.110
Excellent!

495
22:37.730 --> 22:40.180
Then we'll wait for your telegram

496
22:40.450 --> 22:41.940
right here at Xiangbizaiwan.

497
22:41.940 --> 22:45.050
We look forward to our 2 corps joining forces soon.

498
22:45.530 --> 22:46.100
Yes, sir!

499
22:47.860 --> 22:49.790
I guarantee we'll get the job done!

500
22:49.820 --> 22:50.380
Good!

501
22:52.400 --> 22:54.640
Mao, I never expected

502
22:54.970 --> 22:55.940
Comrade Xu Haidong

503
22:55.940 --> 22:58.140
to be so supportive of the Central Committee.

504
22:58.140 --> 22:59.620
He's a straightforward man,

505
22:59.620 --> 23:00.900
with an easygoing nature.

506
23:00.900 --> 23:01.830
I like his style.

507
23:02.250 --> 23:04.650
Unlike his former superior, Zhang Guotao.

508
23:05.020 --> 23:06.540
People like Zhang Guotao

509
23:07.100 --> 23:08.470
are very rare

510
23:08.860 --> 23:10.260
in our Party and our army.

511
23:11.360 --> 23:14.290
With the 15th and 1st Army Corps joining forces,

512
23:15.090 --> 23:18.290
the situation in northern Shaanxi will improve greatly.

513
23:19.820 --> 23:23.780
The men go off to fight, and the women bring them food.

514
23:26.580 --> 23:28.040
Make sure you wash it well!

515
23:29.690 --> 23:30.380
Guoqing.

516
23:30.720 --> 23:31.520
What's wrong?

517
23:31.630 --> 23:33.640
[Zhou Shaolan, Nurse at the 25th Army Corps Hospital]

518
23:32.250 --> 23:33.010
Shaolan,

519
23:34.100 --> 23:35.690
we left Hejiachong

520
23:35.740 --> 23:37.210
last November.

521
23:37.730 --> 23:39.190
It's been a whole year now.

522
23:39.810 --> 23:41.940
I haven't looked in a mirror for a year.

523
23:45.420 --> 23:46.280
Neither have I.

524
23:46.690 --> 23:48.890
I've almost forgotten what I look like.

525
23:50.580 --> 23:52.380
I've gotten thinner and darker.

526
23:52.530 --> 23:53.340
Who says so?

527
23:53.490 --> 23:54.340
To me,

528
23:54.770 --> 23:56.340
you all look even prettier now.

529
23:56.340 --> 23:57.690
Just look at your eyes.

530
23:57.820 --> 23:59.550
They're as bright as the stars.

531
24:00.070 --> 24:00.660
Really?

532
24:02.390 --> 24:03.530
Winter is almost here.

533
24:03.530 --> 24:05.620
After being bundled up, your skin will be fair again.

534
24:05.620 --> 24:07.620
That's right! That's right!

535
24:12.860 --> 24:14.660
Sing some more! Come on!

536
24:14.660 --> 24:16.340
You go first. Your turn.

537
24:16.340 --> 24:17.100
I don't know how.

538
24:17.100 --> 24:18.380
Come on, hurry up!

539
24:18.380 --> 24:18.980
I'll sing.

540
24:19.380 --> 24:23.380
In small Huang'an, everyone's a hero.

541
24:23.620 --> 24:27.620
When the gong sounds, 480,000 rise as one.

542
24:27.690 --> 24:28.420
Beautiful!

543
24:27.800 --> 24:31.820
The men go off to fight, and the women bring them food.

544
24:31.970 --> 24:36.100
The men go off to fight, and the women bring them food.

545
24:40.380 --> 24:42.100
You sing so beautifully!

546
24:43.450 --> 24:44.340
Absolutely!

547
24:45.210 --> 24:46.010
One more time!

548
24:48.860 --> 24:50.900
When the gong sounds,

549
24:50.900 --> 24:52.970
480,000 rise as one.

550
24:53.050 --> 24:55.210
The men go off to fight...

551
24:55.920 --> 25:00.990
[Nanjing, Jiangsu]

552
24:56.100 --> 24:57.590
Intelligence reports indicate

553
24:57.590 --> 24:59.990
that the remnants of the Zhu-Mao forces, driven north,

554
24:59.990 --> 25:02.330
have joined forces with the Communist troops in northern Shaanxi.

555
25:02.330 --> 25:03.570
They are currently lying low

556
25:03.570 --> 25:05.230
around Wayaobu and Yanchang.

557
25:05.420 --> 25:07.210
They appear to be actively rebuilding their forces

558
25:07.210 --> 25:10.010
and expanding the areas under Communist control.

559
25:10.660 --> 25:12.530
My original plan

560
25:12.760 --> 25:14.410
was to drive the Communist troops

561
25:14.410 --> 25:16.250
west of the Luo River and north of the Hulu River,

562
25:16.250 --> 25:17.940
then surround and wipe them out.

563
25:17.940 --> 25:19.340
But Zhang Hanqing (Zhang Xueliang)

564
25:19.340 --> 25:20.490
has been turning a deaf ear,

565
25:20.490 --> 25:22.140
making excuses and disobeying orders.

566
25:22.140 --> 25:24.820
I can't tell whether he genuinely doesn't understand

567
25:24.820 --> 25:26.620
or is deliberately dragging his feet.

568
25:26.620 --> 25:27.940
The most critical element of this plan

569
25:27.940 --> 25:29.100
is speed.

570
25:29.210 --> 25:30.140
But this time,

571
25:30.210 --> 25:33.010
the Northeastern Army has been far too slow to act.

572
25:33.180 --> 25:34.440
Zurong (Yan Daogang),

573
25:34.900 --> 25:37.210
I believe the battles at Laoshan

574
25:37.210 --> 25:38.970
and Yulin Bridge

575
25:39.210 --> 25:40.740
have frightened him badly.

576
25:40.860 --> 25:42.450
Now he's become hesitant and indecisive.

577
25:42.450 --> 25:43.970
I've just signed an order

578
25:44.100 --> 25:47.010
appointing you Chief of Staff of the Northwest Suppression Headquarters.

579
25:47.010 --> 25:48.970
This is a very important appointment.

580
25:48.970 --> 25:50.430
Hanqing is in Nanjing now.

581
25:50.530 --> 25:52.100
There's no need to wait for him.

582
25:52.100 --> 25:53.690
Go to Xi'an and take up your post first.

583
25:53.690 --> 25:55.620
Yes, sir. I'll leave immediately.

584
25:58.010 --> 25:58.660
Madam.

585
26:00.770 --> 26:02.690
When Hanqing arrived in Nanjing today,

586
26:02.690 --> 26:05.690
the only person who went to receive him was Qian Dajun.

587
26:05.770 --> 26:07.970
Everyone was busy, that's why.

588
26:08.860 --> 26:10.940
They were even busier in 1930.

589
26:11.120 --> 26:13.020
When he came to Nanjing for a conference,

590
26:13.020 --> 26:14.290
to welcome him as the newly appointed

591
26:14.290 --> 26:17.100
Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Army, Navy, and Air Force,

592
26:17.100 --> 26:19.100
more than 700 officials turned out.

593
26:19.340 --> 26:21.730
The Pukou Wharf was packed with people.

594
26:22.250 --> 26:24.620
All right, this time I did it on purpose.

595
26:24.900 --> 26:26.860
I sent him to suppress the Communists in northern Shaanxi,

596
26:26.860 --> 26:29.180
but look at him! He's just stood by and done nothing.

597
26:29.180 --> 26:32.290
The Communist forces have grown stronger right under his nose.

598
26:32.290 --> 26:35.100
The situation in northern Shaanxi is now beyond control.

599
26:35.100 --> 26:37.140
I'm giving him the cold shoulder to make him think clearly

600
26:37.140 --> 26:39.140
and see the situation for what it is.

601
26:41.770 --> 26:43.010
All right, all right.

602
26:43.460 --> 26:46.320
With Zurong going to Xi'an to oversee the campaign,

603
26:46.820 --> 26:48.250
you can rest easy now.

604
26:49.340 --> 26:51.100
How can I possibly rest easy?

605
26:52.660 --> 26:54.860
The Japanese are eyeing North China hungrily.

606
26:54.860 --> 26:58.490
The Communist forces marching south seem poised to attack western Sichuan.

607
26:58.490 --> 26:59.290
He Long

608
26:59.490 --> 27:02.860
has launched another breakout attempt along the Hunan-Guizhou border.

609
27:02.860 --> 27:04.660
And then there's Zhang Hanqing.

610
27:05.730 --> 27:06.340
Tell me,

611
27:07.450 --> 27:09.710
isn't trouble breaking out everywhere?

612
27:16.530 --> 27:19.210
You know Hanqing well.

613
27:20.010 --> 27:21.660
He's a real Monkey King.

614
27:22.900 --> 27:24.940
But don't you hold the golden headband

615
27:24.940 --> 27:26.660
that keeps him in check?

616
27:26.970 --> 27:28.250
You can make the headband

617
27:28.250 --> 27:29.580
tighter or looser.

618
27:30.530 --> 27:32.010
It's your call.

619
27:33.480 --> 27:35.940
Zhang Hanqing is simply getting out of hand!

620
27:40.050 --> 27:42.510
If your tooth hurts, you'd better talk less.

621
27:51.120 --> 27:56.250
[Outskirts of Zhiluo Town, Shaanxi; Headquarters of the 1st Red Army Corps]

622
27:54.620 --> 27:56.420
Comrades, dinner's ready!

623
27:56.450 --> 27:57.290
All right, let's eat!

624
27:57.290 --> 27:58.690
Come on, dinner's ready!

625
27:59.070 --> 27:59.620
Let's go eat!

626
27:59.620 --> 28:00.660
Black beans again?

627
28:00.660 --> 28:02.380
I haven't been to the latrine in 3 days!

628
28:02.380 --> 28:02.970
Tell me about it.

629
28:02.970 --> 28:05.530
Black beans just make you bloated. They don't fill you up.

630
28:05.530 --> 28:06.450
We're not getting enough to eat or warm clothes to wear.

631
28:06.450 --> 28:07.530
It's affecting our fighting strength.

632
28:07.530 --> 28:08.210
Exactly!

633
28:08.460 --> 28:09.290
Do we have any steamed corn buns?

634
28:09.290 --> 28:10.180
Even half a bun would do!

635
28:10.180 --> 28:10.940
Could we at least get something different?

636
28:10.940 --> 28:11.730
Exactly!

637
28:11.940 --> 28:12.940
Do we have anything else?

638
28:12.940 --> 28:14.670
We're lucky to have food at all.

639
28:14.690 --> 28:15.620
Hurry up and eat.

640
28:17.380 --> 28:18.100
Comrades,

641
28:18.860 --> 28:20.790
how about I cook something for you?

642
28:20.820 --> 28:22.100
Great!

643
28:22.290 --> 28:24.380
Then I'll make a famous Jiangxi dish.

644
28:24.620 --> 28:25.820
Stir-fried mugwort shoots with cured pork.

645
28:25.820 --> 28:26.310
How does that sound?

646
28:26.310 --> 28:27.770
Great! Sounds delicious!

647
28:27.900 --> 28:28.900
For this dish,

648
28:29.100 --> 28:30.620
the mugwort shoots must be fresh,

649
28:30.620 --> 28:32.660
and the cured pork should be 30% fat and 70% lean.

650
28:32.660 --> 28:34.450
Add a little chili to bring out the flavor.

651
28:34.450 --> 28:36.450
First, fry the pork until fragrant.

652
28:36.570 --> 28:38.580
Then add the mugwort shoots and chili.

653
28:38.580 --> 28:40.140
Sprinkle in a little salt.

654
28:40.420 --> 28:41.250
And finally,

655
28:41.400 --> 28:42.870
just before taking it off the heat...

656
28:42.870 --> 28:44.330
Sneak in a little vinegar.

657
28:44.900 --> 28:45.750
That's right.

658
28:48.220 --> 28:49.680
Sneak in a little vinegar.

659
28:54.440 --> 28:56.230
There's more if anyone wants more!

660
28:56.230 --> 28:57.510
Okay! Okay!

661
28:57.760 --> 28:58.820
Careful, it's hot.

662
28:59.690 --> 29:01.420
According to our earlier deployment,

663
29:01.420 --> 29:03.550
the 1st Red Army Corps has now advanced

664
29:03.690 --> 29:05.580
to the high ground northeast of Zhiluo Town,

665
29:05.580 --> 29:07.450
in the areas of Jiuyuan and Taotong.

666
29:07.450 --> 29:08.580
The main force of the 15th Red Army Corps

667
29:08.580 --> 29:10.010
has advanced to Zhangcunyi

668
29:10.010 --> 29:11.410
and the Taohualing area.

669
29:11.630 --> 29:12.830
Now all we have to do

670
29:12.860 --> 29:15.590
is wait for Dong Yingbin's 57th Army to move east.

671
29:15.780 --> 29:16.900
The biggest problem now

672
29:16.900 --> 29:18.300
is Dong Yingbin himself.

673
29:18.620 --> 29:20.450
Ever since occupying Taibai Town at the beginning of the month,

674
29:20.450 --> 29:21.490
his troops have been hunkering down

675
29:21.490 --> 29:24.490
between Taibai Town and Heshui without making a move.

676
29:26.180 --> 29:27.290
We must be patient.

677
29:28.010 --> 29:29.770
The reason Dong Yingbin isn't moving

678
29:29.770 --> 29:31.700
has less to do with Chiang Kai-shek

679
29:31.860 --> 29:33.100
and more to do with Zhang Xueliang.

680
29:33.100 --> 29:36.340
They took a beating at Laoshan and Yulin Bridge,

681
29:36.860 --> 29:38.580
so they don't dare act rashly.

682
29:42.820 --> 29:45.820
I think we should give them a little push.

683
29:46.380 --> 29:46.940
A push?

684
29:51.010 --> 29:52.660
Order the 15th Army Corps

685
29:52.770 --> 29:54.170
to have its 81st Division

686
29:54.690 --> 29:56.220
step up the siege of Ganquan

687
29:56.530 --> 29:58.060
and make a big show of force.

688
29:58.210 --> 29:59.740
We need to make them believe

689
29:59.860 --> 30:01.970
that the entire main force of the Red Army in northern Shaanxi

690
30:01.970 --> 30:03.500
is laying siege to Ganquan.

691
30:05.970 --> 30:06.700
Understood.

692
30:06.940 --> 30:09.820
I'll send a telegram to the 15th Red Army Corps right away.

693
30:09.820 --> 30:11.100
Take these potatoes.

694
30:11.210 --> 30:11.770
Eat them.

695
30:11.860 --> 30:13.720
I'm sure none of you has eaten yet.

696
30:14.140 --> 30:16.200
Chairman, you haven't eaten either.

697
30:16.380 --> 30:18.040
But there are only 2 potatoes.

698
30:18.140 --> 30:20.670
How are the three of us supposed to share them?

699
30:21.730 --> 30:23.530
Mao, there's something else.

700
30:23.970 --> 30:26.230
The 1st Army Corps is running out of food.

701
30:26.490 --> 30:28.550
Right now, the soldiers

702
30:28.580 --> 30:29.730
are getting only a little coarse grain each day.

703
30:29.730 --> 30:31.100
It's nowhere near enough.

704
30:31.100 --> 30:32.900
And most of our comrades

705
30:33.140 --> 30:35.010
are still wearing thin clothes and straw sandals.

706
30:35.010 --> 30:36.400
They're shivering from the cold.

707
30:36.400 --> 30:39.010
Lin Biao has complained to me several times,

708
30:39.100 --> 30:40.340
saying we can't go on like this.

709
30:40.340 --> 30:41.890
We have to find a solution.

710
30:45.290 --> 30:45.970
Leaders,

711
30:46.180 --> 30:48.140
Chairman Mao, I'd like to report a problem.

712
30:47.060 --> 30:50.030
[Yang Zhicheng, Director of the Logistics Department of the 1st Front Red Army]

713
30:48.780 --> 30:50.530
Securing grain supplies has become extremely difficult.

714
30:50.530 --> 30:51.690
This area is too barren.

715
30:51.690 --> 30:53.160
The local people are very supportive of us,

716
30:53.160 --> 30:55.050
but they're already struggling to get through the winter themselves.

717
30:55.050 --> 30:56.130
They simply have no surplus grain

718
30:56.130 --> 30:56.990
to spare for us.

719
30:57.490 --> 30:58.430
Food is a problem,

720
30:58.430 --> 30:59.820
and clothing and supplies are an even bigger problem.

721
30:59.820 --> 31:01.750
We don't have the money to buy them.

722
31:04.340 --> 31:05.400
Comrade Zhicheng,

723
31:05.770 --> 31:08.430
how much money do we have left?

724
31:09.140 --> 31:10.250
At most,

725
31:11.350 --> 31:12.980
just over 1,000 silver dollars.

726
31:12.980 --> 31:15.510
The 1st Army Corps has over 7,000 men.

727
31:16.690 --> 31:18.970
Even if we stretch every single dollar,

728
31:19.140 --> 31:20.290
it still won't be enough.

729
31:20.290 --> 31:22.950
Even the bravest man is helpless without money.

730
31:25.420 --> 31:27.690
How about I write an IOU

731
31:28.590 --> 31:30.720
and borrow some money from Xu Haidong?

732
31:32.140 --> 31:35.200
I'm just worried they may be short of money themselves.

733
31:36.730 --> 31:37.690
It's worth a try.

734
31:38.010 --> 31:39.210
When you speak to him,

735
31:39.660 --> 31:40.620
make it clear

736
31:40.640 --> 31:42.100
that we don't want to put them in a difficult position.

737
31:42.100 --> 31:43.730
If they can't spare the money,

738
31:43.730 --> 31:44.680
we won't insist.

739
31:45.490 --> 31:46.100
All right.

740
31:46.870 --> 31:49.430
How much should we borrow?

741
31:50.340 --> 31:51.600
2,500 silver dollars.

742
31:55.530 --> 31:57.210
Cutting expenses without finding new sources of income

743
31:57.210 --> 31:59.140
is hardly a sustainable solution.

744
32:00.380 --> 32:02.970
We'll worry about finding new sources of income later.

745
32:02.970 --> 32:04.430
Our top priority right now

746
32:04.590 --> 32:06.790
is to repel the Kuomintang's offensive

747
32:07.660 --> 32:09.390
and make it through the winter.

748
32:14.230 --> 32:20.780
[Daozuopu, Shaanxi; Headquarters of the 15th Red Army Corps]

749
32:15.660 --> 32:16.660
Corps Commander,

750
32:16.920 --> 32:18.240
the lyrics of this song

751
32:18.270 --> 32:20.200
were revised by Comrade Cheng Tan.

752
32:20.950 --> 32:21.820
As for the tune, I adapted it from

753
32:21.820 --> 32:24.210
a song everyone knows

754
32:24.290 --> 32:25.900
in the Hubei-Henan-Anhui Soviet Area,

755
32:25.900 --> 32:27.010
"The Agrarian Revolution Is Complete."

756
32:27.010 --> 32:27.490
Good.

757
32:27.770 --> 32:30.730
The Agrarian Revolution is nearly complete.

758
32:32.180 --> 32:35.380
Every Red Army soldier must remember.

759
32:36.050 --> 32:37.140
Okay. That's good.

760
32:37.180 --> 32:39.100
It's catchy, and everyone knows the tune.

761
32:39.100 --> 32:39.940
Tell them

762
32:40.010 --> 32:41.100
it's not enough just to learn the song.

763
32:41.100 --> 32:43.490
They must also live up to the words.

764
32:43.520 --> 32:47.010
[Liu Huaqing, Section Chief of Enemy Work Department, Political Department of the 15th Red Army Corps]

765
32:44.250 --> 32:44.800
Yes, sir.

766
32:46.600 --> 32:47.930
-Off you go. -All right.

767
32:48.690 --> 32:49.450
Guard!

768
32:49.940 --> 32:50.900
Bring me the map!

769
32:51.100 --> 32:51.730
Yes, sir!

770
32:51.940 --> 32:53.340
Where did all these come from?

771
32:53.340 --> 32:54.820
We captured them from the Northeastern Army.

772
32:54.820 --> 32:55.820
The Corps Commander says

773
32:55.820 --> 32:57.490
we'll soon be fighting the Japanese,

774
32:57.490 --> 32:59.750
so we need to learn about the enemy first.

775
32:59.750 --> 33:00.540
What's this?

776
33:00.690 --> 33:01.820
Is that a submarine?

777
33:01.820 --> 33:02.940
That's a tank.

778
33:03.620 --> 33:04.490
What's this one?

779
33:04.490 --> 33:05.620
And what about this?

780
33:05.690 --> 33:06.770
What about this one? What's this?

781
33:06.770 --> 33:07.980
Can't you read? It's right here.

782
33:07.980 --> 33:09.440
It's an aircraft carrier.

783
33:10.250 --> 33:11.490
It's covered with airplanes.

784
33:11.490 --> 33:12.580
It's enormous!

785
33:13.050 --> 33:14.100
Look at all the smoke coming from its smokestacks.

786
33:14.100 --> 33:15.690
The planes will take off just like that!

787
33:15.690 --> 33:16.580
That's incredible!

788
33:16.580 --> 33:17.180
Look at this.

789
33:17.180 --> 33:18.290
How many planes can it hold?

790
33:18.290 --> 33:18.730
It's absolutely huge!

791
33:18.730 --> 33:22.490
Every Red Army soldier must remember.

792
33:21.250 --> 33:22.180
Are you kidding me?

793
33:22.180 --> 33:23.100
Look how big this is!

794
33:23.100 --> 33:24.140
The river isn't even that wide.

795
33:24.140 --> 33:24.970
Exactly!

796
33:25.820 --> 33:28.290
Even the landlords' mansions aren't that big!

797
33:28.290 --> 33:29.690
Corps Commander. The meal's ready!

798
33:29.690 --> 33:30.290
All right.

799
33:30.730 --> 33:33.330
Save me a flatbread for me. I'll eat it tonight.

800
33:38.730 --> 33:40.660
Comrade, who are you looking for?

801
33:41.000 --> 33:41.810
I...

802
33:42.420 --> 33:43.280
Minister Yang!

803
33:44.290 --> 33:44.850
Come on.

804
33:45.420 --> 33:46.210
Comrade Haidong.

805
33:46.210 --> 33:47.410
What brings you here?

806
33:48.010 --> 33:49.180
You haven't eaten yet, have you? Join us.

807
33:49.180 --> 33:49.900
No, no, no.

808
33:51.380 --> 33:52.300
You've come on orders from above?

809
33:52.300 --> 33:53.500
Chairman Mao sent me.

810
33:54.140 --> 33:54.660
Chairman Mao?

811
33:54.660 --> 33:56.590
Isn't that an order, then? Tell me.

812
33:57.010 --> 33:57.620
Here.

813
34:01.850 --> 34:03.070
The 1st Army Corps is almost out of food.

814
34:03.070 --> 34:05.050
The Central Committee and the Front Army are running low on supplies too.

815
34:05.050 --> 34:06.910
We have no other choice right now.

816
34:11.780 --> 34:12.489
Zha!

817
34:13.340 --> 34:14.260
Zha!

818
34:15.010 --> 34:15.780
Zha Guozhen!

819
34:16.650 --> 34:17.260
Come here!

820
34:20.610 --> 34:22.210
Minister Yang, you're here.

821
34:22.940 --> 34:23.780
Tell me,

822
34:24.010 --> 34:25.880
how much money does our corps have right now?

823
34:25.780 --> 34:28.500
[Zha Guozhen, Head of the Supply Department of the 15th Red Army Corps]

824
34:26.570 --> 34:28.620
At most, 7,000 silver dollars.

825
34:28.820 --> 34:30.050
You're quite the miser,

826
34:30.050 --> 34:31.449
just as your reputation suggests!

827
34:31.449 --> 34:32.710
7,000 silver dollars?

828
34:33.340 --> 34:34.420
Corps Commander,

829
34:34.610 --> 34:36.170
winter is almost here.

830
34:36.340 --> 34:38.130
The cotton clothing our corps needs for the winter,

831
34:38.130 --> 34:38.969
along with medicine,

832
34:38.969 --> 34:41.260
cooking oil, salt, grain and vegetables...

833
34:41.260 --> 34:42.460
By my rough estimate,

834
34:42.570 --> 34:44.520
we'll need at least two or three thousand.

835
34:44.520 --> 34:46.250
And that's still a lot of money.

836
34:46.300 --> 34:48.630
Give Minister Yang 5,000 silver dollars.

837
34:49.219 --> 34:50.219
Comrade Haidong,

838
34:50.570 --> 34:52.610
Chairman Mao is asking to borrow 2,500 silver dollars from you.

839
34:52.610 --> 34:54.820
Would Chairman Mao ask me for help

840
34:55.010 --> 34:56.670
if he weren't in real trouble?

841
34:56.969 --> 34:58.780
The 1st Army Corps has over 7,000 men,

842
34:58.780 --> 35:00.340
not to mention the Central Committee's own staff.

843
35:00.340 --> 35:01.650
What can 2,500 silver dollars

844
35:01.650 --> 35:02.850
possibly do for them?

845
35:08.700 --> 35:09.610
Mao,

846
35:10.090 --> 35:12.170
you asked him for 2,500 silver dollars,

847
35:12.170 --> 35:13.370
but he gave you 5,000.

848
35:13.420 --> 35:15.880
Comrade Xu Haidong is incredibly generous!

849
35:15.900 --> 35:17.740
This isn't about generosity.

850
35:17.740 --> 35:19.870
It's about the bond between comrades.

851
35:20.420 --> 35:22.490
We must remember this kindness.

852
35:24.340 --> 35:25.610
And his generosity

853
35:26.130 --> 35:28.380
goes far beyond these 5,000 silver dollars.

854
35:28.380 --> 35:30.340
Earlier, he and Cheng Zihua

855
35:30.490 --> 35:32.690
held a meeting of cadres in the 15th Army Corps.

856
35:32.690 --> 35:33.860
They ordered every company

857
35:33.860 --> 35:35.340
to contribute 3 machine guns,

858
35:35.340 --> 35:38.130
along with some uniforms, cloth, and medicine,

859
35:38.300 --> 35:39.490
to the 1st Army Corps.

860
35:39.490 --> 35:41.610
He also transferred some soldiers

861
35:41.740 --> 35:44.130
who had enlisted after the battles at Laoshan and Yulin Bridge

862
35:44.130 --> 35:45.930
to reinforce the 1st Army Corps.

863
35:46.050 --> 35:48.650
That's what a true Red Army soldier looks like!

864
35:49.130 --> 35:51.090
There's something else, Chairman Mao.

865
35:51.090 --> 35:52.490
Comrade Xu Haidong suggested

866
35:52.490 --> 35:54.380
that the Central Committee send more cadres

867
35:54.380 --> 35:55.700
to the 15th Army Corps as soon as possible

868
35:55.700 --> 35:56.940
to strengthen its management.

869
35:56.940 --> 36:00.010
Based on the opinions of the leaders,

870
36:00.490 --> 36:02.090
I've drawn up a list of names.

871
36:02.860 --> 36:05.380
We're planning to send Zhou Shidi, Wang Shoudao,

872
36:05.380 --> 36:07.170
Feng Wenbin, Song Shilun,

873
36:07.170 --> 36:08.220
and Huang Zhen

874
36:08.610 --> 36:09.940
to serve with the 15th Army Corps.

875
36:09.940 --> 36:11.470
Do you have any objections?

876
36:13.090 --> 36:14.870
Agreed. No objections.

877
36:15.780 --> 36:17.450
Our immediate difficulties have been eased for now.

878
36:17.450 --> 36:19.940
Next, we just have to wait for the Northeastern Army

879
36:19.940 --> 36:21.340
to enter our encirclement.

880
36:21.340 --> 36:21.910
Exactly.

881
36:24.860 --> 36:26.340
Meanwhile, as the 1st Front Red Army

882
36:26.340 --> 36:27.530
waited patiently for an opportunity

883
36:27.530 --> 36:29.570
around Zhiluo Town,

884
36:30.700 --> 36:32.740
the 4th Front Red Army, marching south,

885
36:32.740 --> 36:34.490
followed the previously established

886
36:34.490 --> 36:37.170
Suining-Danba-Chonghua-Maogong Campaign Plan.

887
36:37.170 --> 36:38.530
They successively repelled attacks by Sichuan Army,

888
36:38.530 --> 36:40.740
including those under Yang Sen and Liu Wenhui,

889
36:40.740 --> 36:43.140
amounting to approximately 17 regiments.

890
36:43.220 --> 36:46.170
They captured the county seats of Danba and Maogong,

891
36:46.380 --> 36:49.880
as well as key strategic locations including Fubian, Suijing, Chonghua,

892
36:49.880 --> 36:52.780
Dawei, and Rilongguan.

893
36:53.420 --> 36:54.950
At this point, Zhang Guotao

894
36:55.220 --> 36:58.940
had become completely carried away by these temporary victories.

895
36:58.940 --> 37:00.570
He went on to launch another campaign,

896
37:00.570 --> 37:01.570
targeting Tianquan, Lushan,

897
37:01.570 --> 37:02.610
Mingshan, Ya'an,

898
37:02.610 --> 37:04.530
as well as Qionglai and Dayi.

899
37:04.760 --> 37:05.950
Although the 4th Front Red Army

900
37:05.950 --> 37:07.430
fought bravely

901
37:08.050 --> 37:12.110
and successively captured Baoxing, Tianquan, Lushan, and other areas,

902
37:12.340 --> 37:15.050
with its vanguard advancing toward the Western Sichuan Plain,

903
37:15.050 --> 37:17.570
its officers and soldiers had been fighting continuously

904
37:17.570 --> 37:19.380
and were now utterly exhausted.

905
37:19.490 --> 37:22.350
Their combat effectiveness had declined sharply.

906
37:22.420 --> 37:24.170
And what lies ahead of them

907
37:24.450 --> 37:28.510
is a well-prepared elite Sichuan Army numbering hundreds of thousands.

908
37:40.580 --> 37:44.510
[Renjiaba, Lushan County, Sichuan; Headquarters of the 4th Front Red Army]

909
37:41.090 --> 37:41.830
Comrades,

910
37:43.000 --> 37:44.710
we have now captured

911
37:44.890 --> 37:47.570
Tianquan and Lushan.

912
37:48.220 --> 37:50.530
Next, we must seize this opportunity

913
37:50.650 --> 37:52.580
while the enemy is still in retreat

914
37:52.740 --> 37:55.780
and hasn't had time to regroup.

915
37:56.010 --> 37:57.540
We must press our advantage

916
37:57.610 --> 37:58.810
and capture Mingshan,

917
37:58.810 --> 38:01.130
Ya'an, Qionglai, and Dayi,

918
38:01.490 --> 38:03.930
thus carrying out our original strategic plan.

919
38:02.750 --> 38:03.890
[Zhang Guotao, Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Politburo,]

920
38:03.890 --> 38:04.460
[Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,]

921
38:04.460 --> 38:05.040
[General Political Commissar of the Red Army]

922
38:05.700 --> 38:06.740
Commander-in-Chief,

923
38:06.740 --> 38:07.570
you're late.

924
38:13.650 --> 38:15.860
I was just telling the comrades

925
38:16.670 --> 38:18.380
that the troops defending Tianquan County

926
38:18.380 --> 38:20.420
were led by Guo Xunqi of the Sichuan Army.

927
38:20.270 --> 38:23.600
[Xu Xiangqian, Commander-in-Chief of the 4th Front Army]

928
38:20.700 --> 38:22.450
I know you two go way back.

929
38:22.960 --> 38:24.260
Back in Tucheng,

930
38:24.340 --> 38:26.220
Guo Xunqi put up quite a fight.

931
38:26.070 --> 38:28.230
[Chen Changhao, Director of the Red Army's General Political Department,]

932
38:26.290 --> 38:28.810
I heard he even forced Commander-in-Chief Zhu

933
38:28.230 --> 38:30.400
[Political Commissar of the 4th Front Army]

934
38:28.860 --> 38:30.810
to gallop straight

935
38:31.010 --> 38:32.740
to the front lines himself!

936
38:33.260 --> 38:34.320
But look at him now.

937
38:34.830 --> 38:36.700
In the end, we drove Guo Xunqi

938
38:36.940 --> 38:38.570
into a humiliating retreat!

939
38:38.740 --> 38:39.490
Well?

940
38:40.450 --> 38:42.090
Our 4th Front Red Army

941
38:42.170 --> 38:43.940
has avenged you.

942
38:48.010 --> 38:49.090
Just now,

943
38:49.610 --> 38:50.900
Comrade Guotao

944
38:51.940 --> 38:53.010
said I was late.

945
38:54.220 --> 38:55.530
Do you know why?

946
38:58.650 --> 39:00.260
Let me show you something.

947
39:06.450 --> 39:07.820
I just took

948
39:08.170 --> 39:09.860
these straw sandals

949
39:09.860 --> 39:11.060
off a soldier's feet.

950
39:11.090 --> 39:12.420
His name was Li Ersheng.

951
39:12.780 --> 39:14.420
You may not know him.

952
39:14.830 --> 39:17.510
He was from Cangxi County, Sichuan.

953
39:17.780 --> 39:19.800
He served in the 1st Squad, 1st Platoon,

954
39:19.800 --> 39:23.060
Reconnaissance Company, 263rd Regiment, 88th Division.

955
39:23.710 --> 39:24.500
He died.

956
39:26.300 --> 39:28.360
He was literally exhausted to death.

957
39:29.300 --> 39:31.650
His own brother, Li Daniu,

958
39:31.940 --> 39:33.340
also died in the battle

959
39:33.970 --> 39:37.460
to capture Tianquan County, which just ended.

960
39:38.780 --> 39:39.910
On the very same day.

961
39:40.940 --> 39:41.780
Two brothers.

962
39:42.610 --> 39:43.420
Comrades,

963
39:44.170 --> 39:45.340
we've won

964
39:45.970 --> 39:47.280
quite a few battles lately.

965
39:47.280 --> 39:48.410
That's a good thing.

966
39:48.530 --> 39:49.700
And it's certainly worth celebrating.

967
39:49.700 --> 39:50.570
It shows that

968
39:50.570 --> 39:51.820
our 4th Front Red Army

969
39:51.820 --> 39:53.480
has a fierce fighting spirit.

970
39:53.870 --> 39:54.750
But

971
39:55.380 --> 39:56.820
we mustn't let victory go to our heads.

972
39:56.820 --> 39:58.740
We need to face reality.

973
39:58.970 --> 40:02.610
Since the Suijing-Chonghua-Danba-Maogong

974
40:02.940 --> 40:04.500
campaign began,

975
40:05.050 --> 40:08.300
our troops have been fighting continuously for over a month.

976
40:08.300 --> 40:09.210
Before that,

977
40:09.780 --> 40:13.380
many units had already crossed the grasslands twice

978
40:13.480 --> 40:15.570
and climbed over several snow-capped mountains.

979
40:15.570 --> 40:17.300
Our men are utterly exhausted.

980
40:17.620 --> 40:19.890
If we continue marching south,

981
40:20.380 --> 40:22.010
from Tianquan and Lushan

982
40:22.130 --> 40:23.570
toward Ya'an,

983
40:23.820 --> 40:26.020
we'll enter the Western Sichuan Plain.

984
40:26.180 --> 40:28.780
That is the heartland of the Sichuan warlords!

985
40:29.090 --> 40:31.090
If we push deep into that territory,

986
40:31.170 --> 40:33.970
they will surely throw everything they have at us

987
40:34.170 --> 40:35.420
to stop our advance.

988
40:35.650 --> 40:38.380
Besides, the terrain there is completely flat,

989
40:38.450 --> 40:41.420
making it difficult for our troops to take cover or defend against air raids.

990
40:41.420 --> 40:43.260
Can an army as exhausted as ours

991
40:43.450 --> 40:45.220
really make it through?

992
40:45.590 --> 40:47.190
So, I suggest

993
40:48.100 --> 40:50.780
that we consider suspending our southward advance

994
40:50.780 --> 40:53.940
and resting for a while

995
40:53.970 --> 40:55.420
around Tianquan, Lushan, and Baoxing

996
40:55.420 --> 40:57.520
before deciding on our next move.

997
40:58.010 --> 40:59.900
The Western Sichuan Plain is vast.

998
40:59.900 --> 41:00.860
Advancing recklessly

999
41:00.860 --> 41:02.370
could do us more harm than good.

1000
41:02.370 --> 41:03.090
Exactly.

1001
41:03.170 --> 41:04.970
Our soldiers are physically exhausted, too.

1002
41:04.970 --> 41:07.030
Speak up if you have something to say.

1003
41:08.050 --> 41:09.910
Let's hear everyone's thoughts.

1004
41:10.170 --> 41:11.050
I believe

1005
41:11.340 --> 41:12.780
we should press on

1006
41:12.940 --> 41:13.570
and capture Mingshan, Ya'an,

1007
41:13.570 --> 41:14.750
Qionglai, and Dayi in one swift campaign.

1008
41:14.750 --> 41:16.470
Just as the General Political Commissar said before,

1009
41:16.470 --> 41:18.380
we'll march all the way to Chengdu and feast on rice!

1010
41:18.380 --> 41:19.050
Exactly!

1011
41:19.340 --> 41:21.400
I believe we should strike hard and fast in battle.

1012
41:21.400 --> 41:22.130
Besides,

1013
41:22.220 --> 41:24.170
Hu Zongnan and Zhou Hunyuan have already headed north

1014
41:24.170 --> 41:25.940
to pursue Mao, Zhang, and Zhou.

1015
41:26.310 --> 41:27.900
Wu Qiwei has gone to western Hunan.

1016
41:27.900 --> 41:29.230
That leaves only Li Baobing's troops

1017
41:29.230 --> 41:30.360
and the Sichuan Army

1018
41:30.610 --> 41:31.860
in all of Sichuan.

1019
41:32.130 --> 41:33.300
The Sichuan Army

1020
41:33.430 --> 41:34.460
is no match for us!

1021
41:34.490 --> 41:35.130
Exactly!

1022
41:35.570 --> 41:37.170
The General Political Commissar is right.

1023
41:37.170 --> 41:38.120
We've already breached

1024
41:38.120 --> 41:39.490
the gateway to the Western Sichuan Plain.

1025
41:39.490 --> 41:42.280
We've laid the groundwork for establishing the Sichuan-Xikang Soviet Area.

1026
41:42.280 --> 41:43.270
What does that prove?

1027
41:43.270 --> 41:46.400
It proves our southward offensive strategy is correct.

1028
41:48.570 --> 41:49.490
Comrades,

1029
41:49.820 --> 41:52.090
I ask you to step outside

1030
41:52.260 --> 41:53.700
and take a look at the streets.

1031
41:53.700 --> 41:54.940
Look at what our soldiers

1032
41:54.940 --> 41:56.730
have become.

1033
41:57.420 --> 41:58.740
How many more soldiers like Li Ersheng

1034
41:58.740 --> 42:00.390
do we have to sacrifice?

1035
42:02.670 --> 42:03.540
Can we

1036
42:05.830 --> 42:07.560
really keep fighting this war?

1037
42:27.570 --> 42:28.650
Comrade Guotao,

1038
42:30.170 --> 42:31.420
what's your opinion?

1039
42:50.660 --> 42:52.720
Why not fight one decisive battle...

1040
42:56.520 --> 42:57.940
and settle the matter once and for all?
